## Cron schedule examples

Used by **Build periodically** and **Poll SCM**. The format is `minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week`.

| Schedule | Expression | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Every minute | `* * * * *` | Runs once every minute. |
| Every 5 minutes | `*/5 * * * *` | Runs every 5 minutes. |
| Every 10 minutes | `*/10 * * * *` | Runs every 10 minutes. |
| Every 15 minutes | `*/15 * * * *` | Runs every 15 minutes. |
| Every 30 minutes | `*/30 * * * *` | Runs every 30 minutes (twice per hour). |
| Every 2 minutes (hashed start) | `H/2 * * * *` | Runs every 2 minutes, with job-specific offset (balanced load). |
| Every 5 minutes (hashed start) | `H/5 * * * *` | Runs every 5 minutes, staggered per job. |
| At minute 0 (top of every hour) | `0 * * * *` | Runs at the start of every hour. |
| At minutes 0 and 30 | `0,30 * * * *` | Runs twice every hour (at 0 and 30 minutes). |
| At minutes 5, 20, 35, and 50 | `5,20,35,50 * * * *` | Runs 4 times each hour at specified minutes. |
| Between 10 and 20 minutes past each hour | `10-20 * * * *` | Runs every minute between 10 and 20 past the hour. |
| Every 10 minutes between 9 AM and 5 PM | `*/10 9-17 * * *` | Runs every 10 minutes, only during working hours. |
| Every minute on weekdays (Mon–Fri) | `* * * * 1-5` | Runs every minute Monday through Friday. |
| Every 15 minutes on weekends | `*/15 * * * 6,0` | Runs every 15 minutes only on Saturday and Sunday. |
| Every 10 minutes on weekdays, 9 AM–6 PM | `*/10 9-18 * * 1-5` | Runs every 10 minutes during office hours, Monday–Friday. |
| Once every hour at random minute | `H * * * *` | Runs hourly at a unique, consistent minute for each job. |
| Every 2 hours (corrected) | `H */2 * * *` | Runs every 2 hours. |
| Every hour | `H * * * *` | Runs once every hour. |
| Every day at midnight | `H 0 * * *` | Runs daily at midnight. |
| Every weekday at 9 AM | `H 9 * * 1-5` | Runs Monday to Friday at 9 AM. |
| Every 15 minutes | `H/15 * * * *` | Runs every 15 minutes. |
| Every Sunday at 2 AM | `H 2 * * 0` | Runs weekly on Sunday 2 AM. |
| On the 1st of every month at 5 PM | `H 17 1 * *` | Runs monthly on the 1st at 5 PM. |
| Twice a day (at 6 AM and 6 PM) | `H 6,18 * * *` | Runs two times per day. |

> **Correction:** your original table listed `H/2 * * * *` as "Every 2 hours". That expression runs every **2 minutes**. Every 2 hours is `H */2 * * *`.

