## Pipeline project

### 1. General

| Option | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Discard old builds | Automatically deletes old build history to save disk space. |
| Do not allow concurrent builds | Allows only one build at a time. A new build waits until the previous one finishes |
| Do not allow the pipeline to resume if the controller restarts | If Jenkins restarts while the pipeline is running, the pipeline will not continue from where it stopped. |
| GitHub project | Links the Jenkins job to the GitHub repository/project. |
| Pipeline speed/durability override | Controls the balance between pipeline performance and reliability when Jenkins is restarted. |
| This project is parameterised | Allows you to provide input values when starting the build, such as `ENV_NAME=QA`, `BROWSER=chrome`, etc. |
| Throttle builds | Limits how many builds of this job can run at the same time, based on configured throttling rules. Time period like seconds, minutes and hours etc. |

### 2. Triggers

Same options as the Freestyle project: remote trigger, build after other projects, build periodically, GitHub hook trigger, Poll SCM. See [Cron schedule examples](#cron-schedule-examples).

