## Real-time pipeline features

| # | Feature | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Clean Workspace | Avoids stale files: `deleteDir()` |
| 2 | Parallel Browser Testing | Runs Chrome + Edge at the same time: `parallel { Chrome ; Edge }` |
| 3 | Retry Failed Tests | Reduces flaky test failures in real teams: `retry(1)` |
| 4 | Publish TestNG HTML Report | Visible in the Jenkins UI |
| 5 | Archive Screenshots | Selenium screenshots stored automatically: `archiveArtifacts 'target/screenshots/**'` |
| 6 | Build management | Prevents concurrent builds, keeps logs for the last 10 builds, and times out jobs after 30 minutes |
| 7 | HTML Reports | Professional display inside Jenkins |

**To make this fully work, your project must support:**

- `-Dbrowser=chrome` and `-Dbrowser=edge`, read in your Selenium `BaseTest`:
  ```java
  String browser = System.getProperty("browser", "chrome");
  ```
- Screenshots saved to `target/screenshots`

### Example script ★ (Maven + Selenium + TestNG)

Adjust the tool names to match **Manage Jenkins → Tools**.

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    options {
        disableConcurrentBuilds()
        buildDiscarder(logRotator(numToKeepStr: '10'))
        timeout(time: 30, unit: 'MINUTES')
        timestamps()
    }

    stages {
        stage('Clean Workspace') {
            steps { deleteDir() }
        }

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps { checkout scm }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps { bat 'mvn clean compile -DskipTests' }
        }

        stage('Run Tests') {
            parallel {
                stage('Chrome') {
                    steps { retry(1) { bat 'mvn test -Dbrowser=chrome' } }
                }
                stage('Edge') {
                    steps { retry(1) { bat 'mvn test -Dbrowser=edge' } }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            junit allowEmptyResults: true, testResults: 'target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
            publishHTML(target: [
                reportDir: 'target/surefire-reports',
                reportFiles: 'index.html',
                reportName: 'TestNG HTML Report',
                keepAll: true,
                alwaysLinkToLastBuild: true,
                allowMissing: true
            ])
            archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'target/screenshots/**', allowEmptyArchive: true
        }
    }
}
```

> **Watch out:** Chrome and Edge run in the same workspace, so both write to `target/`. If their reports overwrite each other, give each run its own report folder.

