## Troubleshooting

Errors from your own builds, with the fix for each ★.

| Error or symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `Cannot run program "powershell"` | The Jenkins service can't find `powershell.exe` | Use `bat` instead of `powershell`, or add `C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0` to PATH and restart Jenkins |
| `No Allure installation found` | The plugin is installed but the Allure tool is not | Manage Jenkins → Tools → Allure → Add Allure → install automatically |
| `unexpected token: }` or other Groovy errors | Syntax error in the Jenkinsfile, for example `git branch: 'main',` with no `url` | Fix the syntax. The error names the line number. |
| Jenkins runs an old version of the Jenkinsfile | Jenkins reads the file from GitHub, not from VS Code | `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, then rebuild |
| Parameters don't show on the first build | Jenkins registers them after the first run | Run once, then use **Build with Parameters** |
| `Tool type "nodejs" does not have an install of "NodeJS-20"` | The tool name doesn't match | Match the name in Manage Jenkins → Tools exactly |
| `No SCM` with `checkout scm` | The script was pasted into the job | Use **Pipeline script from SCM**, or use the `git` step with your URL |
| Playwright says no tests found | Wrong spec path or no matching tag | Check the file path and the tag in the test title |
| Headed mode shows no browser window | The Jenkins service has no desktop | Use headless, or run the agent in a logged-in desktop session |
| Allure report is empty | `allure-results` had no files | Check the Playwright stage ran tests and the `allure-playwright` reporter is set |